<title>GERMANY: German growth won't help jobs - stats office.</title>
<headline>German growth won't help jobs - stats office.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Federal Statistics Office said on Thursday that German economic growth was insufficient to curb unemployment significantly.</p>
<p>&quot;Our real growth in 1996 was 1.4 percent, that was below productivity growth of 2.5 percent,&quot; the office's president Johann Hahlen told Reuters at a news conference in Wiesbaden.</p>
<p>&quot;From our point of view, that cannot have a positive impact on the labour market. We need real growth exceeding productivity growth, then we can expect the labour market to benefit,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
